# Vulnerabilities govulncheck may report without failing CI.
#
# Format: one OSV id per line, everything after # is a comment. scripts/
# govulncheck.sh reads this file and fails on any reachable finding that is not
# listed here.
#
# An entry states why the finding does not apply, how that was checked, and a
# review date. Remove the entry as soon as the finding stops being reported.
# An entry is never a way to carry a real vulnerability past CI: if the finding
# applies, fix the dependency instead.

GO-2026-6909
#   Module:  github.com/crewjam/saml, reported against ParseXMLResponse, which
#            internal/http_handlers/saml_sp.go does call.
#   Status:  FALSE POSITIVE. Both vulnerabilities it describes are fixed in the
#            v0.6.2 we build against. The OSV record is what is wrong: its
#            affected range is `{"introduced": "0"}` with no `fixed` event, so
#            govulncheck treats every published version as affected, while the
#            advisory text itself says "through v0.5.1".
#   Checked: read the two sites in the module cache, v0.5.1 against v0.6.2.
#            1. Nil-pointer in validateAssertion: v0.5.1 declares
#               `Issuer *Issuer` (schema.go) and dereferences
#               `assertion.Issuer.Value` with no nil check
#               (service_provider.go:1185). v0.6.2 declares `Issuer Issuer`, a
#               value, so the dereference at service_provider.go:2124 cannot
#               panic.
#            2. Namespace-blind Subject.NameID: v0.5.1 declares
#               `NameID *NameID` with NO xml tag (schema.go:799), so
#               encoding/xml matches <NameID> in any namespace. v0.6.2 declares
#               `NameID *NameID` tagged
#               `xml:"urn:oasis:names:tc:SAML:2.0:assertion NameID"`
#               (schema.go:1251), so a foreign-namespace element no longer
#               populates it.
#   Action:  the fix is upstream in the OSV data, not here. Report the missing
#            `fixed` event on https://github.com/golang/vulndb/issues/6909 and
#            drop this entry once the range is corrected.
#   Review:  2026-12-08
